From 9a4311aa64dfb6ed09237a38d879f56ca3cb029f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:00:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Galaxigans: the fixed shooter, ported to the game pane

A port of the Mojo GalaxigansDeluxe, which is the complete port of
MACVM's Galaxigans, which ported the x64 assembler original. Every
constant is that original's, down to the 8x5 formation on a 56x34 grid,
the dive whose random seed IS the flight plan, and the 30 Hz step it was
tuned at.

What the Mojo pane does in four layers this does in four. The twelve
cosmos are layer 0 -- the shader is verbatim, only its entry point is
ours, and the scene arrives in parameter 0 so twelve skies cost one
compile. The indexed world carries the sparks, the shots and the tractor
beam. The fleet are sprites, each of the fourteen species with sixteen
colours of its own, which is what the sprite palettes were for. The HUD
is the front plane, over the sprites, so an alien crossing the score
passes behind it.

The beam is the piece worth having built all this for: the cone is drawn
once in palette index 1, and index 1 means something different on every
scanline, so its colour flows downward without a pixel being redrawn.

The creature library and the shader are generated from the Mojo sources
by script rather than retyped -- 1069 lines of art nobody should transcribe
by hand.

